-- title:
--   Origin-chart ideals detected by their formal-chart images
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring which is local, Noetherian and complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $T$. Write $\mathcal{O}$ for `OriginChartRing W`, the degree-zero part of the homogeneous localization away from the coordinate `coord W 1` (the variable $Y$) of the graded ring $T[X_0,X_1,X_2]/(F_W)$, $F_W$ the Weierstrass cubic of the projective model, with its grading `projModelGradingCR W` induced from the homogeneous grading. Let $\Phi : \mathcal{O} \to T\llbracket X\rrbracket$ be a ring homomorphism subject to three normalisations: $\Phi$ sends the image of each scalar $t \in T$ under the structure map into degree $0$ to the constant series $\mathrm{C}\,t$; $\Phi(\,$`xOverY W`$\,) = -X$, where `xOverY W` is the degree-zero fraction $X_0/X_1$; and $\Phi(\,$`zOverY W`$\,) = -\,$`W.formalW`, where `zOverY W` is $X_2/X_1$ and `W.formalW` is the Weierstrass series $w(X)$ obtained as the coefficientwise limit of the iterates of the substitution `W.wSubst` from $0$. Put $\mathfrak{p} = \Phi^{-1}(\mathfrak{m}_{T\llbracket X\rrbracket})$. Then for all ideals $I, J$ of $\mathcal{O}$ whose images generate the same ideal of $T\llbracket X\rrbracket$, the ideals generated by $I$ and by $J$ in the localization $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{p}}$ coincide.
--
--   This is the statement that the formal chart at the origin detects ideals of the origin chart of a Weierstrass curve up to germs at the origin point: equality of the readings of two ideals in $T\llbracket X\rrbracket$ forces equality of their germs in the local ring at $\mathfrak{p}$. It is used in the comparison of the Drinfeld divisor with the $q$-torsion subscheme, where both chart ideals have the same image under $\Phi$.
